# construction/domain-registry.bron -- domains held, as a record a program can read.
#
# WHY THIS FILE. Naming decisions in this tree keep reaching for a domain, and a domain either is
# held or is not. Recording them once means a naming round checks a file rather than a memory --
# the same reason the standing-equipment roster stopped living in a paragraph. Several names this
# tree already uses appear here, and a few names here have no module yet, which is the useful part.
#
# ROOM. `construction/` is withheld from the public seed by absence from the allowlist, which is
# right for an ownership record: each name is public on its own, and the portfolio with terms and
# intent is business material rather than documentation.
#
# ONE ENTRY IS NOT HELD. `199999999999.net` reads EXPIRED 20260710 in the account listing. It stays
# in the record with its status rather than being dropped, because a registry that silently omits
# what lapsed teaches a reader the wrong thing about what the account contains. `held` counts the
# rest.
#
# SOURCE. Squarespace account domain list, 20260823, A-Z, given verbatim by Keaton as a Zig
# payload of 126 entries. Held here in Bron, the tree's own data notation, so a Rishi tool reads it
# without a parser of its own.

format domain-registry-v1
stamp 20260823.114751
source squarespace account domain list 20260823 a-z
listed 126
expired 1
held 125

domain 199999999999.net           role EXPIRED 20260710 -- listed by the account, no longer held
